---
import UtilityLayout from "../../layouts/UtilityLayout.astro";
import UtilityApp from "../../components/UtilityApp.astro";
---

<UtilityLayout
  title="CSV to nested JSON"
  description="Map CSV columns into nested JSON, group repeated rows, and review every mapping before converting locally."
  slug="csv-to-nested-json"
>
  <UtilityApp tool="csv" />
  <section class="prose">
    <h2>Group CSV rows without writing a transformation script</h2>
    <p>
      A flat converter creates one JSON object per row. This tool also supports
      grouping a parent record and collecting child records into one array.
      Paste one representative parent object as the desired shape; each leaf
      becomes an editable source-column mapping.
    </p>
    <h2>Example: one customer, several items</h2>
    <p>
      Repeated Customer values such as 001 become one parent. Map SKU to
      items[].sku and Qty to items[].quantity. Every child row is retained,
      including duplicates. Conflicting parent values and blank grouping keys
      are rejected rather than silently dropped.
    </p>
    <h2>Scope and limits</h2>
    <p>
      Up to 20 columns, 10,000 rows, nested objects and one child-array path.
      All values remain strings: quantities are not coerced, and leading-zero
      identifiers remain intact. Constants, arbitrary scripts, multiple child
      arrays, automatic deduplication and general schema inference are not
      supported. Jev proposes a mapping from your example and instructions; you
      remain responsible for reviewing it.
    </p>
  </section>
</UtilityLayout>
